      "severity": "CONCERN",
      "title": "Avoid interpolating already-expanded queries again during execution",
      "description": "The new call expands template variables before splitting, but `LokiDatasource.runQuery()` delegates to `DataSourceWithBackend.query()`, which calls `applyTemplateVariables()` again. Shard splitting adds another expansion in `shardQuerySplitting.ts` before reaching this code.\n\nInterpolation is not idempotent: if `$service` has the literal value `$other`, the first pass inserts `$other` into the selector, and the execution-time pass resolves it as another variable. Enabling splitting can therefore change the query\u2019s meaning and return different results from ordinary execution.\n\nEnsure each target is interpolated only once while still making expanded expressions and steps available to the splitting logic. Add a regression test exercising the backend request path with a variable value containing a dollar-prefixed variable name; the added tests mock `runQuery()`, so they bypass the additional interpolation.",
